<title>BELGIUM: Belgian Bayer unit, unions reach draft deal.</title>
<headline>Belgian Bayer unit, unions reach draft deal.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Striking workers at Agfa-Gevaert NV, the Belgian photographic products unit of German chemicals group Bayer AG, were expected to resume work on Wednesday, a trade union spokesman said on Monday.</p>
<p>He told BRTN radio that a draft agreement, reached between management and unions earlier on Monday, was likely to be accepted by workers in a referendum on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The workers went on strike last Thursday after talks to renew a collective workers agreement (CAO) broke down.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6815, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
